# dispatch-and-waits: an ordinary clause allows only after its Guard tests
# have dispatched successfully. Its pass then climbs as an ordinary message.
# A matching wait for allows before a deciding Handler's veto, so that veto
# has no open Verdict. An unmatched message allows at the end of its path.

